    "body": "Thank you, @sn3ro, for the clear use case (Ø11 × 7 counterbores, Ø6 flat end mill, light mill). Triage: `enhancement`, `P6`, `effort:high` (a new toolpath strategy; under our safety floor), `area:2d`. The helix must keep the existing Bore checks: the wall radius must leave room for the tool (refuse when hole radius − tool radius − stock-to-leave is too small for a helix), the ramp angle must respect the tool's limits, and the floor circle must not gouge a model floor. Claim it with a `claimed:` comment if you want to take it.",
